Track 1: One Streetlamp Before Home
- Song Description: A worker facing redundancy spends one final lunch break beneath the crane where an entire adult life has been measured in whistles and overtime. The song resolves not with heroic escape but with the worker taking one small tool home and finally admitting fear about starting again. Musically, Ion-Tide should shape the scene through Detuned Roland JP-8000 (for the "Euro" leads), custom-built electromagnetic ring-drums, and low-tuned acoustic marimbulas., with the arrangement moving from concrete environmental detail toward a decisive final image. Keep the emotional register grounded in the established emotional tension rather than abstract declarations; each verse must change the situation, and the chorus should turn a physical detail from the title into the song’s central memory.

